# Build context is the repo root; both deploy Dockerfiles end with a
# broad COPY . . — everything listed here stays OUT of the images.
# Audit infra H1: production .env files (database URL, session/MFA/data
# keys, provider secrets) were baked into image layers this way.

# Secrets and environment files (the committed template stays).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# VCS metadata — large, useless at runtime, and a history leak.
.git
.github

# Runtime data is a mounted volume in production, never image content.
runtime-data
**/runtime-data

# Dependencies are installed inside the image from the lockfile.
**/node_modules

# Build outputs and caches are produced inside the image.
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
